{"id":3914,"date":"2021-10-25T13:57:33","date_gmt":"2021-10-25T20:57:33","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=3914"},"modified":"2025-10-23T13:25:13","modified_gmt":"2025-10-23T20:25:13","slug":"1-8-remote-control-junior-cde-blockly","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/1-8-remote-control-junior-cde-blockly\/","title":{"rendered":"1.8: Remote Control"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22135096033\" name=\"6a22135096033\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>We've Moved!<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1761251110572{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-11766\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/icon_warning-150x150-2-84x85.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"81\" height=\"82\" \/><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><strong>We\u2019ve moved to our new lesson portal: <a href=\"http:\/\/learn.robolink.com\">Robolink Learn<\/a>! Lessons here will remain available until the end of June 2026. This version of Basecamp will no longer be updated and uses outdated references to Blockly for Robolink. You can access the previous version of <a href=\"https:\/\/codrone.robolink.com\/edu\/blockly-archive\/\">Blockly here<\/a>.<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213509617f\" name=\"6a2213509617f\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Set LED<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1739924502427{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-11766 alignleft\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/icon_warning-150x150-2-84x85.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"106\" height=\"107\" \/><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><strong>KEYBOARD BLOCK USE HAS BEEN UPDATED<\/strong><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\">The functionality of keyboard presses has been updated so it is compatible with Blockly and matches Python behavior. Please make sure to read through this lesson to learn how they work. Read the rest of the updates on our<a href=\"https:\/\/docs.robolink.com\/docs\/CoDroneEDU\/Blockly\/Blockly-Changelog\"> release notes.<\/a><\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_column_text]Make sure that your drone is connected with <a href=\"https:\/\/codrone.robolink.com\/edu\/blockly-archive\/\">Blockly<\/a> before starting the lesson! If you are unsure of how to connect, go back to <a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/0-1-connecting-and-coding-with-cde-blockly\/\">the first lesson<\/a> to review![\/vc_column_text][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You may be wondering how to use the keyboard to control CoDrone EDU. In this activity, you will learn how to use conditionals to control your LED and flight movements. Start your program with the light off so you can turn it on later by inputting commands with the keyboard.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12187&#8243; img_size=&#8221;412&#215;134&#8243; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221350961ea\" name=\"6a221350961ea\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Forever Loop<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Since you want your program to constantly check if you are pressing a key, you will need to implement a <strong>forever loop<\/strong>. For this example, use a <strong>repeat loop<\/strong> block and connect a <strong>true<\/strong> block from the &#8220;Logic&#8221; menu. <\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12176&#8243; img_size=&#8221;495&#215;360&#8243; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22135096247\" name=\"6a22135096247\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Get keyboard input<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Now it&#8217;s time to check for keyboard input! Go to the &#8220;Events&#8221; category and insert a <strong>get key press<\/strong> block in your loop.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;13409&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This block will request user input in the console. When you type in a letter and press &#8220;Enter&#8221; on your keyboard, it will save as your keyboard input.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221350962bf\" name=\"6a221350962bf\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Conditional<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Next, add the conditional <strong>if<\/strong> statement block from the &#8220;Logic&#8221; category and connect it to the <strong>when key press<\/strong> block from the &#8220;Events&#8221; category. This block allows you to input single character key presses:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>numbers 0-9<\/li>\n<li>letters a-z<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>The default value selected is &#8216;0&#8217; (zero). Right now, this feature only works for single characters.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;13413&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Now use the dropdown to change the key to &#8216;r&#8217; and make the drone LED turn red.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;13414&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<h3><strong>Important!<\/strong><\/h3>\n<p>Include an extra &#8220;else if&#8221; statement to break from the loop. For example, if you input &#8216;q&#8217; (q for quit!) then the loop will break and the program will stop.<\/p>\n<p>Add your<strong> break out of loop<\/strong> block from the &#8220;Loops&#8221; category. Then, test your program. Input &#8216;r&#8217; and then input &#8216;q&#8217;.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;13416&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213509631e\" name=\"6a2213509631e\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>More Keys<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you want to check for multiple key presses, you will need to include an else if statement for each new key. Add four new else if statements:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>when &#8216;w&#8217; key press<\/li>\n<li>when &#8216;a&#8217; key press<\/li>\n<li>when &#8216;s&#8217; key press<\/li>\n<li>when &#8216;d&#8217; key press<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;13418&#8243; img_size=&#8221;664&#215;815&#8243; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22135096369\" name=\"6a22135096369\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Adding Flight Commands<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Now add flight movements. Use the go block from &#8220;Flight Commands&#8221; to add 4 movements. We recommend forward, backward, left, and right to get started.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;13419&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221350963b5\" name=\"6a221350963b5\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Add takeoff and land<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Don&#8217;t forget the <strong>take off<\/strong> block! This block should go before the while loop. If it&#8217;s inside the while loop, the drone will keep sending the takeoff over and over again.<\/p>\n<p>The land block needs to also go outside of the loop at the very bottom. When you press &#8216;q&#8217;, the loop will break and the drone will land![\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;13420&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22135096412\" name=\"6a22135096412\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 9<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenge<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div><strong>Challenge: Reverse Controller<\/strong><\/div>\n<div>For this challenge, let&#8217;s challenge your mind. Write a keyboard controller with all the controls reversed. For example, the &#8216;w&#8217; key will move the drone backward and the &#8216;s&#8217; key will move the drone forward.<\/div>\n<div><\/div>\n<div>Build an obstacle course and try to fly to the finish line using your reverse controller. If you need to, adjust the values of the delays and add more keys for more functionality!<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213509645a\" name=\"6a2213509645a\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 10<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Lesson Complete<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]In this lesson, you learned how to program your very own remote using all the blocks you have learned about so far. You also had the chance to design your own obstacle course to test your flight skills with your custom controller![\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7547&#8243; img_size=&#8221;750&#215;670&#8243; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 11 We've Moved! [vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1761251110572{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}\"] We\u2019ve moved to our new lesson portal: Robolink Learn! Lessons here&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/1-8-remote-control-junior-cde-blockly\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":4741,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":3877,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1814,1760,1817,1763,1777,1737,1815,1793,626,1533,1438,853,144,167,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2135,2108,4328,14401,2121,2122,2111],"class_list":["post-3914","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-beginner","lesson-tag-blockly","lesson-tag-cde","lesson-tag-cdej","lesson-tag-keyboard","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-remote-control","module-beginner","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3914","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":40,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3914\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":13622,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3914\/revisions\/13622"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/4741"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=3914"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=3914"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=3914"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}